# The research corpus index is the retrieval layer for 332 external papers and
# MUST travel with the repo: every session queries it instead of ~/Downloads,
# which has returned EPERM and silently produced zero-hit searches.
!data/research_corpus_index.json

# g128 canonical set, register J17. data/* is ignored, so these must be
# un-ignored or J15 becomes unreproducible again.
!data/g128_2026-08-18/
!data/g128_2026-08-18/**

# g128 velocity/depth sweeps, register J18.
!data/g128_sweeps_2026-08-18/
!data/g128_sweeps_2026-08-18/**

# Open-channel in/outflow BC validation, 2026-08-18. data/* above is a
# blanket ignore, so a new data directory needs this explicit pair or it silently
# never travels.
!data/openchannel_2026-08-18/
!data/openchannel_2026-08-18/**

# Phase 1 of the two-phase corpus ingest, added 2026-08-20. An agent turn holding
# the Undermind connector writes the deep-search records here and the plain-shell
# builder in analysis/research_index.py reads them, because that builder is pure
# standard library and cannot call an MCP connector. These files are the ONLY
# route by which 13 of the project's 21 completed deep searches reach the corpus
# at all, so they must survive a clone and a worktree. That is the whole point:
# they were invisible for five weeks precisely because nothing tracked them.
!data/deep_searches/
!data/deep_searches/**

# The external centre-of-mass falsifier's output. Small, and it is the first
# gate result in this project that can fail for a reason outside the pipeline.
!data/cm_floor_check.json
